{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>רחש</b> — His heart will speak the words of the poet. And some say: words that he brings forth from his heart, and this psalm was spoken about David or about the Messiah his son, for so is his name, \"and David My servant shall be prince over them forever.\"" "<b>מעשי</b> — This is the song that he made."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The phrase וזה המזמור נאמר could read 'and this psalm is said'; rendered past tense following the idiom of biblical citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:51.663998425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}